{
  "id": "software-license-enterprise",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "name": "Enterprise Software License and Support Agreement",
  "description": "Negotiated on-premises software license — a perpetual or term grant in object code, with maintenance and support, source-code escrow, an acceptance test, a software warranty and an IP indemnity. Distinct from `eula`, which lints a click-through end-user form under EU consumer law, and from `copyright-license`, which reads a § 106 grant of works. Carries no ruleset of its own; it selects the always-on commercial packs with the columns an enterprise license actually has.",
